# What the build context may contain, as an allowlist.
#
# **`applications/` went to a remote builder before this existed.** The image
# was clean -- the Dockerfile copies three paths and nothing else -- but the
# *context* is uploaded whole, and that context was 118 MB across 11,704 files:
# `.git` 49 MB, `.claude` 33 MB, and `applications/` 9.4 MB of real resumes and
# cover letters carrying a real name, address, phone number and email. None of
# it belonged on a builder disk.
#
# **Deny everything, then allow, rather than the other way round.** A denylist
# is a list somebody has to remember to extend, and the thing it forgets is by
# definition the thing nobody thought of. `.gitignore` in this repository is a
# denylist and it is exactly why `applications/` unanchored once swallowed an
# API route: a pattern written for one purpose matching somewhere else. Here
# the default is out, and a new directory of anything is out until named.
*

# The three paths the Dockerfile copies, and nothing else. Each needs its
# parent un-ignored before its contents can be.
!scripts/
!scripts/**
!packages/
!packages/**
!docs/
docs/*
!docs/write-paths.md

# And re-deny what should never travel even from inside those, because
# `scripts/` holds working files the repository does not track.
scripts/_*
scripts/**/__pycache__/
scripts/**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store
